deathdruid wrote:
> Having lost my last three Valks to random wands of death before
> Medusa, I was hoping for something better this time around. Lo and
> behold, I reach level 12 and see a black dragon disintegrating
> monsters left and right. How does one get reflection so early? I have
> done Sokoban and got the bag of holding. Any other tips on getting
> past the black dragon are welcome. AFAICS my only option is to dig
> down past the level with the dragon, and that just seems like it is
> putting off a known problem for other black dragons or wands of death.

I suppose it's either a shapeshifter (a chamaeleon) or some monster
that stepped into a polytrap. In the first case the problem will
disappear soon; wait until it gets something wimpy and kill it.
In the second case you can't do anything simple; dig through to the
next level, as you say, or try to lock the dragon in a room that has
only doors and no open doorways. If you're tough enough (I suppose
you're not at that stage) you may also decide to try to kill him by
melee; on melee range (it might be a bit tricky to get adjacent) the
dragon won't breath. Later there's a chance (25%/75%) that you find
a shield of reflection at Medusa's isle. You know, if you manage to
kill the dragon and eat the corpse you'll become immune to his breath.

